</article>$$f: S→S'$ is a monoidal left Quillen functor between model categories satisfying the hypotheses of Proposition \ref{enrichcatper}, with right adjoint $g: S' →S$. Then $f$ and $g$ induce a Quillen adjunction \[  \xymatrix {\SCat  \ar @< .4ex>[r]^{ F} &amp;  \Cat _{\mathbf{S}'}, \ar @< .4ex>[l]^{G}} \] where $F$ and $G$ are as in Remark \ref{laxcon}. Moreover, if $(f,g)$ is a Quillen equivalence, then $(F,G)$ is likewise a Quillen equivalence. $<article class="env-remark" id="">
