  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F14D54">Definition <span data-tag="F14D54">8.3.2.9</span>.</a> Let </p>
</article>$$S$ be a monoidal model category, and let $$ be a $S$-enriched category. We will say that a morphism $f$ in $$ is an {\it equivalence} if the homotopy class $[f]$ of $f$ is an isomorphism in $h <em>$.\index{gen}{equivalence!in a }$S$-enriched category$</em> 
</p>
<p>
We will say that $$$ is {\it locally fibrant} if, for every pair of objects $X,Y $, the mapping space $_(X,Y)$ is a fibrant object of $S$.\index{gen}{fibrant!locally}\index{gen}{locally fibrant} 

We will say that a 

$S$-enriched functor $F: →'$ is a {\it local fibration}\index{gen}{fibration!local} if the following conditions are satisfied: \begin{itemize} \end{itemize}$
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(i)$"><p>
For every pair of objects $$X,Y $, the induced map $_(X,Y) →_'(FX,FY)$ is a fibration in $S$. \item [$(ii)$] The induced map $h <em> →h <em>'$ is a quasi-fibration of categories. $</em></em>
</p>
