  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/49EA73">Remark <span data-tag="49EA73">8.3.2.10</span>.</a> Let </p>
</article>$$F: →'$ be a functor between $S$-enriched categories which satisfies condition $(i)$ of Definition \ref{twurp}. Let $X $ and $Y '$ be objects. If $'$ is locally fibrant, then every morphism $[f]: F(X) →Y$ in $h <em>'$ can be represented by an equivalence $f: F(X) →Y$ in $'$. Let $Y$ be an object of $$ such that $F( Y = Y$. Since $<strong>1</strong>_S$ is a cofibrant object of $S$ and the map $_( X, Y ) →_( F(X), Y)$ is a fibration, Proposition \ref{princex} implies that $[f]$ can be lifted to an isomorphism $[f]: X →Y$ in $h <em>$ if and only if $f$ can be lifted to an equivalence $f: X →Y$ in $$. Consequently, when $h <em>$ is locally fibrant, condition $(ii)$ is equivalent to the following analogous assertion: \begin{itemize} \end{itemize}$</em></em></em>
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii')$"><p>
For every equivalence $$f: F(X) →Y$ in $'$, there exists an equivalence $f: X →Y$ in $$ such that $F( f ) = f$. $
</p>
